1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
=Godslayer=
(Adapted from the novel Godslayer.)

2
00:00:33,125 --> 00:00:36,916
(Divine Era, Lunisolar Calendar,
Waxing Gibbous)

3
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,708
(There is a beast)

4
00:00:38,708 --> 00:00:40,083
(with five tails and one horn.)

5
00:00:40,083 --> 00:00:41,541
(It is called the Zheng.)

6
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,708
(Only bitter candy can awaken
its true five-tailed form.)

7
00:00:43,708 --> 00:00:44,583
(And only once in its lifetime.)

8
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:45,875
(My name is Duo Mu.)

9
00:00:46,125 --> 00:00:47,250
(I have five tails.)

10
00:00:47,916 --> 00:00:49,000
(Yan told me)

11
00:00:49,166 --> 00:00:50,666
(not to let people see them.)

12
00:00:51,875 --> 00:00:52,708
(I listen to Yan.)

13
00:00:59,916 --> 00:01:00,666
Yan.

14
00:01:00,666 --> 00:01:01,625
Kiddo.

15
00:01:07,416 --> 00:01:07,958
Sir,

16
00:01:07,958 --> 00:01:09,291
draw the three of us.

17
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:16,416
(During the Ascension Trial,)

18
00:01:17,166 --> 00:01:18,416
(a mirror hangs in the sky,)

19
00:01:19,291 --> 00:01:21,000
(showing the trials
throughout the Capital.)

20
00:01:21,166 --> 00:01:22,667
(The people of the Upper, Middle,
and Lower Cities)

21
00:01:22,667 --> 00:01:23,791
(Ascension Temple of Middle City)
(The people of the Upper, Middle,)

22
00:01:23,791 --> 00:01:24,791
(Ascension Temple of Middle City)
(and Lower Cities)

23
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:27,333
(can all watch)

24
00:01:27,791 --> 00:01:30,041
(the battles in the arena.)

25
00:01:33,166 --> 00:01:34,416
It's broad daylight.

26
00:01:34,708 --> 00:01:36,166
Why light so many candles in here?

27
00:01:38,416 --> 00:01:39,625
Without a burning candle,

28
00:01:39,958 --> 00:01:41,166
the room stays dark.

29
00:01:44,583 --> 00:01:46,416
Then why trim the wick?

30
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:49,625
Trim the wick,

31
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:52,291
and the candle burns brighter.

32
00:01:54,708 --> 00:01:56,541
Is this the Middle City's
Ascension Office?

33
00:01:56,875 --> 00:01:58,125
We're here to ascend.

34
00:01:59,125 --> 00:02:01,708
The Ascension Tablet is at the summit.

35
00:02:01,708 --> 00:02:03,666
For the Middle City trial,

36
00:02:03,666 --> 00:02:05,583
there is only one rule.

37
00:02:10,583 --> 00:02:12,458
Three incense sticks is the limit.

38
00:02:12,958 --> 00:02:14,958
No death, no end.

39
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:22,500
True Lord,

40
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:24,208
there's something I don't understand.

41
00:02:24,708 --> 00:02:27,041
The Ascension Trials have always been
decided in a single fight.

42
00:02:27,458 --> 00:02:29,125
Why give them two extra chances?

43
00:02:30,083 --> 00:02:31,708
One fight to the death?

44
00:02:32,625 --> 00:02:35,500
That's nothing more than a blood sport
for the arena.

45
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,833
This time,

46
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:40,291
we're putting on a show that breaks them
before it kills them.

47
00:02:40,666 --> 00:02:41,833
Killing them is easy.

48
00:02:42,875 --> 00:02:45,791
Breaking their spirit is the hard part.

49
00:02:47,291 --> 00:02:48,458
Hurry up!

50
00:02:48,458 --> 00:02:49,875
It's already started!

51
00:02:49,875 --> 00:02:50,875
Is it set yet?

52
00:02:55,458 --> 00:02:56,375
There!

53
00:02:56,875 --> 00:02:58,458
Keep it right there.

54
00:02:58,583 --> 00:02:59,500
Quick, light the incense.

55
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:00,583
Match the timing over there.

56
00:03:27,375 --> 00:03:28,166
Race?

57
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:28,440
Hmph.

58
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:29,375
You're on.

59
00:03:29,875 --> 00:03:30,791
Three...

60
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:32,040
Hey!

61
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,250
He jumped the start!

62
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,083
♪You bent the iron ring underfoot,
then turned and said, "Keep up"♪

63
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:36,916
What if you lose?

64
00:03:37,166 --> 00:03:38,000
Loser's a dog.

65
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
♪I kept the blade low
and heard my heartbeat roar♪

66
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,458
♪Her vines lashed across the mountain.
Green light chased the clouds♪

67
00:03:42,458 --> 00:03:45,290
♪Three shadows, one behind the other,
turned the dangerous road into a thrill♪

68
00:03:45,295 --> 00:03:48,300
♪With the boy from Dazedi,
crashing through every storm♪

69
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:50,830
♪One candy hadn't even melted,
and you'd already leapt past the clouds♪

70
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:53,880
♪What's the difference between
the Monster Wastes and the Capital?♪

71
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,300
♪With friends by your side,
any road is worth the race♪

72
00:03:56,310 --> 00:03:58,400
♪Run. Don't look back above the clouds♪

73
00:03:58,410 --> 00:04:01,200
♪Laughter sweeps past
mountains and seas, never ending♪

74
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:03,541
♪The moment the cold glaze cracks,
there's light♪

75
00:04:03,541 --> 00:04:04,250
Here.

76
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:06,083
Wow!

77
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:06,833
That's awesome!

78
00:04:07,792 --> 00:04:09,950
♪Run, while your heart still burns♪

79
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:12,900
♪While your friends
are still beside you♪

80
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:15,050
♪If one day you think of me♪

81
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:22,250
♪Think of this reckless joy♪

82
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:28,291
One strike, one kill!

83
00:04:28,458 --> 00:04:29,958
I knew they could do it!

84
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:30,875
Easy.

85
00:04:31,083 --> 00:04:32,000
Hold still.

86
00:04:37,416 --> 00:04:38,416
That's it?

87
00:04:38,541 --> 00:04:40,416
They're not even as good as
the father-and-son duo from the Qi Clan.

88
00:05:06,625 --> 00:05:09,000
Aren't Porcelain Armored Soldiers
unable to revive once they're beheaded?

89
00:05:09,833 --> 00:05:11,166
How are they not only coming back,

90
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:12,250
but also

91
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:13,458
turning into monsters?

92
00:05:16,291 --> 00:05:18,416
That gong is controlling them.

93
00:05:18,458 --> 00:05:19,416
One strike, one command.

94
00:05:19,666 --> 00:05:20,458
As long as the gong keeps sounding,

95
00:05:20,583 --> 00:05:21,416
the runes stay active.

96
00:05:21,416 --> 00:05:22,208
Then how do we fight them?

97
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:24,208
We take out whoever's sounding
that gong first.

98
00:05:24,666 --> 00:05:25,375
I'll do it.

99
00:05:49,375 --> 00:05:50,916
Those who trespass

100
00:05:51,666 --> 00:05:52,583
die!

101
00:05:53,291 --> 00:05:54,375
Ugly fool.

102
00:05:54,875 --> 00:05:56,125
You talk too much.

103
00:10:33,916 --> 00:10:35,375
(Middle City Ascension Trial.)

104
00:10:35,375 --> 00:10:37,041
(Three incense sticks is the limit.)

105
00:10:37,041 --> 00:10:38,916
(No death, no end.)

106
00:10:39,083 --> 00:10:40,291
(The three-incense limit means)

107
00:10:40,791 --> 00:10:42,333
(when the third incense stick
burns down,)

108
00:10:42,958 --> 00:10:45,083
(the Challengers lose.)

109
00:10:46,166 --> 00:10:48,958
(One Challenger must give their life)

110
00:10:49,458 --> 00:10:51,250
(to earn a second chance.)

111
00:10:51,833 --> 00:10:55,583
(That is what "No death, no end" means.)

112
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,833
A young hero,

113
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:10,375
watching his companions

114
00:11:10,458 --> 00:11:12,458
die one by one before his eyes...

115
00:11:13,458 --> 00:11:14,666
That look in his eyes

116
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:17,041
will surely please the gods.

117
00:11:18,083 --> 00:11:19,083
Duo Mu.

118
00:11:19,833 --> 00:11:21,333
I'll hold them off.

119
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:23,291
Find an opening and get out of here.

120
00:11:27,750 --> 00:11:28,500
Yan.

121
00:11:44,833 --> 00:11:45,500
Yan.

122
00:11:58,750 --> 00:11:59,875
(Without a burning candle,)

123
00:12:00,375 --> 00:12:01,500
(the room stays dark.)

124
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:05,500
(Trim the wick,)

125
00:12:06,208 --> 00:12:08,583
(and the candle burns brighter.)

126
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,250
♪I carry the name you gave me♪

127
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:19,700
♪Through every desolate, empty place♪

128
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
♪That faint glimmer in your eyes♪

129
00:12:23,541 --> 00:12:24,041
Yan.

130
00:12:25,625 --> 00:12:26,792
When you're alive,

131
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:28,792
you need something sweet.

132
00:12:28,792 --> 00:12:29,583
=Episode 8=
(Stay Alive. Stay Sweet.)

133
00:12:29,583 --> 00:12:30,580
♪I wish for a heart still blazing♪

134
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:34,880
♪I'll warm the shadows
and the cold within your heart♪

135
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,860
♪I'll be here watching over you♪

136
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,440
♪No matter how long the night may be♪

137
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:46,840
♪I'll stay right by your side♪

138
00:12:48,450 --> 00:12:48,875
♪I don't ask how endless the road is♪

139
00:12:48,875 --> 00:12:49,875
Duo Mu!

140
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,291
♪Wait till all regrets have settled♪

141
00:12:58,291 --> 00:12:59,041
(The Zheng has five tails.)

142
00:12:59,333 --> 00:13:00,416
(With one tail, mountains bow.)

143
00:13:01,541 --> 00:13:02,666
(With two, rivers yield.)

144
00:13:02,666 --> 00:13:04,666
♪I'll go with you to the faraway♪

145
00:13:04,666 --> 00:13:05,500
(With three, seas overturn.)

146
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:09,750
(With four, cities fall.)

147
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,200
♪Let the sweetest candy♪

148
00:13:12,375 --> 00:13:13,250
(With all five unleashed,)

149
00:13:13,541 --> 00:13:15,041
(Heaven and Earth bow.)

150
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:19,460
♪Even if we're worlds apart♪

151
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:24,200
♪Please don't forget to wait for me
to come home♪

152
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:26,120
♪With the longest dream♪

153
00:13:27,458 --> 00:13:29,291
(Then why do you only have one tail?)

154
00:13:31,250 --> 00:13:32,791
(When I eat that bitter candy,)

155
00:13:32,916 --> 00:13:33,916
(you'll see them.)

156
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:39,000
♪Please don't forget to take me home♪

157
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,940
♪Home♪

158
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:54,240
♪I follow the path you took♪

159
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:57,520
♪Through all the long years
along the way♪

160
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:01,080
♪That little smile upon your lips♪

161
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:04,320
♪Is the most beautiful sight
I've ever seen♪

162
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:08,560
♪I'd be a ray of moonlight in the night♪

163
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,880
♪To melt away the pain you carry♪

164
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:17,160
♪And lay it all to rest for you♪

165
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,340
♪No matter how vast the world may be♪

166
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,900
♪With you here by my side♪

167
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:28,140
♪No dream can frighten me♪

168
00:14:34,375 --> 00:14:37,208
(But I can only do it once in my life.)

169
00:14:37,541 --> 00:14:39,458
(So I'm not going to waste it.)

170
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,720
♪Come with me to lands far away♪

171
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:50,080
♪Let the sweetest candy♪

172
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:54,820
♪Become the moonlight in your heart♪

173
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:57,400
♪Even if we're worlds apart♪

174
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:02,500
♪Please don't forget to wait for me
to come home♪

175
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:04,200
♪With the longest dream♪

176
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:09,480
♪I'll wipe away all your tears♪

177
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:11,920
♪When I scatter into a river of stars♪

178
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:17,020
♪Please don't forget to take me home♪

179
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,320
♪Home♪

180
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,160
♪I follow the path you took♪

181
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:35,860
♪Through all the long years
along the way♪

182
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:39,380
♪That little smile upon your lips♪

183
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:42,600
♪Is the most beautiful sight
I've ever seen♪

184
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:46,250
So?

185
00:15:46,583 --> 00:15:48,708
Did I look cool back there?

186
00:15:50,333 --> 00:15:51,458
A five-tailed Zheng.

187
00:15:51,958 --> 00:15:52,666
Very cool!

188
00:15:53,791 --> 00:15:54,750
Actually,

189
00:15:55,333 --> 00:15:56,416
I've always wanted

190
00:15:56,833 --> 00:15:58,250
to look cool just once.

191
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:00,291
Duo Mu!

192
00:16:01,208 --> 00:16:01,958
What's wrong with him?

193
00:16:03,833 --> 00:16:05,083
It's the bitter candy.

194
00:16:06,125 --> 00:16:07,500
It's made from bitterroot

195
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:09,208
and the blood
of a scorpion-tail monster.

196
00:16:09,875 --> 00:16:10,791
Once consumed,

197
00:16:11,208 --> 00:16:12,958
it draws out all the body's
vital essence,

198
00:16:13,375 --> 00:16:15,291
burning through the strength
of every organ.

199
00:16:15,916 --> 00:16:18,041
His monster power surges
for a short time,

200
00:16:18,916 --> 00:16:20,041
but afterward,

201
00:16:20,625 --> 00:16:22,083
his organs will fail.

202
00:16:22,583 --> 00:16:23,875
Not even the gods can save him.

203
00:16:25,250 --> 00:16:27,625
Bitter candy...

204
00:16:28,625 --> 00:16:31,041
Then can't he just eat something sweet
to cancel it out?

205
00:16:32,208 --> 00:16:33,208
Didn't you say

206
00:16:33,208 --> 00:16:33,833
if you're alive,

207
00:16:33,833 --> 00:16:35,291
you need something sweet?

208
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:37,500
Then why did you eat the bitter one?

209
00:16:40,250 --> 00:16:41,708
Kiddo.

210
00:16:44,166 --> 00:16:45,541
The sweet ones

211
00:16:47,458 --> 00:16:49,083
are for you.

212
00:16:53,166 --> 00:16:54,166
Yan...

213
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:57,833
Yan...

214
00:16:59,000 --> 00:16:59,666
I'm here.

215
00:17:00,791 --> 00:17:01,916
The bitter candy

216
00:17:04,041 --> 00:17:05,583
wasn't bitter at all.

217
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:09,700
♪Please don't forget to call me home♪

218
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:11,360
♪With words left unspoken♪

219
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:16,620
♪Answer all the hearts
that still long for me♪

220
00:17:17,083 --> 00:17:18,000
Duo Mu!

221
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:24,560
♪Please don't forget to take me home♪

222
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:28,710
♪Home♪

223
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:33,680
♪Home♪

224
00:17:38,125 --> 00:17:39,416
(The three incense sticks
have burned out.)

225
00:17:40,125 --> 00:17:42,166
(A Challenger's life has been exchanged
for another round.)

226
00:17:42,791 --> 00:17:44,291
(The trial resumes tomorrow.)

227
00:18:25,041 --> 00:18:26,666
(Yan... Kiddo...)

228
00:18:40,916 --> 00:18:41,833
(Kiddo.)

229
00:18:41,833 --> 00:18:42,625
(Nice teamwork.)

230
00:18:42,625 --> 00:18:43,625
(This is for you.)

231
00:18:44,625 --> 00:18:46,041
(The Ascension Trials take teams
of three.)

232
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:47,708
(One person costs 300 crystals.)

233
00:18:47,833 --> 00:18:49,541
(Three people cost the same.)

234
00:18:50,208 --> 00:18:51,666
(Might as well get our money's worth.)

235
00:19:01,708 --> 00:19:02,916
Redtail Armed Escort Agency.

236
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,208
A promise across a thousand miles.

237
00:19:06,583 --> 00:19:07,791
Redtail Armed Escort Agency.

238
00:19:09,833 --> 00:19:11,041
A promise kept through life and death.

239
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:14,250
We send our brother

240
00:19:14,250 --> 00:19:15,458
home in triumph!
